> "I personally prefer the ridged solitaire for men who do hands-on work. The ridges add grip and the band feels more secure. The grooved version is better for suits and formal wear. Same diamond, same gold, two different personalities." — Farzana Hasan, [diamond expert](/about-farzana)

### Look 3 — Channel Band

A channel band sets a row of diamonds in a recessed track along the top of the ring. The stones sit flush with the metal surface — no prongs, no snagging on clothing.

This is the most practical look for daily wear. The channel setting protects the girdles of the stones. The diamonds sit below the metal rim, shielded from direct impact on all sides.

You can wear a channel-set ring through most physical activity. The stones face no risk.

